  "notes": "{目立|めだ}つ means to stand out or be conspicuous. It's formed from {目|め} (eye) + {立|た}つ (to stand).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Something stands out on its own\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {目立|めだ}つ{色|いろ}: conspicuous color\n- {目立|めだ}たない: inconspicuous, not noticeable\n- {目立|めだ}って: noticeably, conspicuously\n- {目立|めだ}ちたがる: to want to stand out\n\nEXAMPLES:\n- {赤|あか}い{服|ふく}は{目立|めだ}つ: Red clothes stand out\n- {傷|きず}が{目立|めだ}つ: The scratch is noticeable\n- あまり{目立|めだ}たないように: so as not to stand out\n\nRELATED:\n- {目立|めだ}たない: inconspicuous\n- {派手|はで}: flashy, showy",
